# BusinessSuite ERP — Mobile responsive (Capacitor-ready)

Every authenticated and public surface must work on phone-width viewports so the same Next.js UI can ship inside Capacitor.

## Navigation (mandatory)

- Desktop: fixed left accordion sidebar (`SidebarNav`).
- Mobile (`< lg`): hamburger opens a full-height **slide-over drawer** with the same accordion (modules + children). Overlay closes the drawer; navigating closes it.
- Do not use a horizontal module-chip strip as the only mobile nav.
- Keep top **GlobalMenuSearch** (under header on small screens). Touch targets ≥ ~44px for menu / chevron / close.
- Respect `env(safe-area-inset-*)` on header, drawer, main, and dialogs.

## Layout & overflow

- Root shell and `body`: `overflow-x: hidden`; use `min-h-[100dvh]` where full height matters.
- Page content: `bs-page` + `min-w-0` so flex/grid children don’t blow past the viewport.
- Wide tables: wrap in `overflow-x-auto` (or rely on `.bs-card` / `.bs-page table` mobile rules in `globals.css`). Prefer stacking form grids (`grid` → `md:grid-cols-*`) over fixed multi-column layouts on phones.
- Toolbars, subnav chips (`AdminSubnav`), confirm actions: stack or scroll horizontally; full-width primary buttons on the smallest breakpoint when it helps tap accuracy.

## Viewport / Capacitor

- Keep Next.js `viewport` export with `width=device-width`, `viewportFit: "cover"`, and sensible `themeColor` in `app/layout.tsx`.
- Prefer `100dvh` over `100vh` for shell chrome.
- Inputs: `touch-action: manipulation` (already on form controls in `globals.css`); avoid hover-only critical actions.

## When adding pages

1. Use shared shell / breadcrumbs / UI primitives — don’t invent fixed-width layouts.
2. Test mentally at ~375px: nav reachable, no horizontal page scroll, tables scroll inside cards, forms usable.
3. Module subnavs / action rows must wrap or scroll; never force a desktop-only sidebar pattern on mobile.
